Third-party files in this repository (everything else is original, MIT, see LICENSE).
All of them live under crates/retro-m68k/vendor/ .
crates/retro-m68k/vendor/shim/ is ours (MIT): freestanding libc stubs so Musashi builds for CoralOS.

Musashi 4.60, Copyright Karl Stenerud, MIT-style permission notice kept in each file header:
  m68k.h  m68kcpu.c  m68kcpu.h  m68k_in.c  m68kmake.c
  m68kconf.h   (MODIFIED by us: ILLEGAL and per-instruction callbacks are set to
                retro_illg_hook / retro_instr_hook, plus extern prototypes)
  m68kcpu.h    (MODIFIED by us: m68ki_exception_1010 first asks retro_aline_hook, so a host can handle classic Mac
                A-line traps itself)

Removed 2026-10-17: Musashi's MAME-derived m68kfpu.c and m68kmmu.h (MAME-team copyright, MAME licence). They are
replaced by crates/retro-m68k/vendor/m68k_nofpu.h (ours, MIT): the engines run a 68020 with no FPU and no PMMU, which
traps those opcodes (F-line) exactly as the stubs do. m68kcpu.c is MODIFIED by us at its include of those two files.

SoftFloat Release 2b, John R. Hauser (via MAME packaging), own terms in its README:
  softfloat/README.txt  softfloat/mamesf.h  softfloat/milieu.h  softfloat/softfloat.c
  softfloat/softfloat.h  softfloat/softfloat-macros  softfloat/softfloat-specialize
  (mamesf.h is SoftFloat's porting/typedef header as packaged by MAME; SoftFloat terms.)
  Terms (read 2026-10-17, softfloat.c header): derivative works are acceptable, even commercially, if the
  source carries prominent notice that it is derivative and retains the four legal paragraphs. The files
  are unmodified and keep those paragraphs.

No Amiga ROM, AROS, Workbench or Apple code is included. Struct offsets and LVO numbers
are written from public NDK-style documentation and must be re-verified against a
licence-checked source before they are relied on (see docs in the CoralOS plan).

crates/mac68k-engine/src/trap_names.rs: trap words and names are interface facts, generated by tools/gen-trap-names.py
from metamage_1's relix/files/etc/traps; no code from it (or from executor / macemu) is included.

crates/retro-raster/src/topaz8.rs: AROS topaz 8 font data (rom/graphics/default_font.c, charData/charLoc), Copyright (C) 1995-2026
The AROS Development Team, AROS Public License (APL); the file keeps that header. Data only.
crates/mac68k-engine, crates/retro-resfork: low-memory addresses, QDGlobals layout, the MENU/WIND resource layouts, MacBinary and
AppleDouble layouts are interface facts read from metamage_1 (v68k-lowmem, ams-qd, ams-seg, macbinary) and executor's source
(wind, menu, appledouble), cited in the file headers; no code from them is included. Executor's apps (packages/go) are used only as
test inputs read from the reference tree, not copied into this repository.

crates/retro-pef: the PEF container format (headers, loader section, pattern-data and relocation opcodes, export hash) is
written from Apple's "Mac OS Runtime Architectures" facts, cross-read against Apple's CFMLateImport sample (opcode
numbering, TVector12/8 strides) and Executor's MIT cfm.cpp / pef_hash.cpp (hash word, pattern data semantics); no code
from them is included. Executor's loader implements RelocSmRepeat (chunk rewind, which ours matches) but asserts on RelocLgRepeat/LgSetOrBySection; ours implements all three.

crates/retro-theme/src/uifont_data.rs: Nunito Sans Regular bitmap strip (generated), Copyright 2016 The Nunito Sans Project Authors (https://github.com/Fonthausen/NunitoSans), SIL Open Font License 1.1.

